error: rsjs boundary: `rsjs::island(...)` cannot declare or read parent `signal(...)` state

       Why:
         Explicit child islands are independent client scopes. State must belong to the parent island or the child island, not both through the boundary expression.

       Use one of:
         - Declare the state in the parent and keep the reactive markup in the parent island.
         - Declare independent state inside the child island.
         - Pass plain server data across the island boundary and coordinate later through query, mutation, or custom events.

       Tracked feature:
         server_boundary.state_declaration
  --> tests/ui/conformance/fail/40_island_state_declaration.rs:30:61
   |
30 |                 {rsjs::island(ChildWithServerValue { value: signal(0_i64).get() })}
   |                                                             ^^^^^^
